# Smart Rename (iurysza/herdr-tab-smart-rename), installed by run_after_53.
#
# RULES-ONLY BY DEFAULT, BUT THIS FILE ALONE DOES NOT ENFORCE IT. The plugin
# names tabs from deterministic process rules with no model call at all, and
# only reaches for a model when those rules find the work ambiguous. That second
# path has TWO activation sources, and a key from either one turns it on:
#
#   1. A key set in this file.
#   2. A key INHERITED from the environment herdr itself was launched with.
#      herdr passes its own environment through to a plugin, and the plugin
#      reads a process key exactly as it reads a file key. So an OPENAI_API_KEY
#      or SMART_RENAME_API_KEY exported for some other tool activates the model
#      path here with no edit to this file at all.
#
# RULES-ONLY THEREFORE REQUIRES BOTH: no key here, AND neither OPENAI_API_KEY nor
# SMART_RENAME_API_KEY in herdr's process environment. v0.2.0 has no explicit
# model-off switch, so absence is the only lever. Checked on dresden: neither
# variable appears in dot_bashrc.tmpl, in any LaunchAgent plist, under
# ~/.config/herdr, or in any running herdr process.
#
# The five settings below are the plugin's own defaults, recorded so the shape
# of a provider is visible without reading its source.
SMART_RENAME_PROVIDER=openai
SMART_RENAME_BASE_URL=https://api.openai.com/v1
SMART_RENAME_MODEL=gpt-5.6-luna
SMART_RENAME_REASONING_EFFORT=medium
SMART_RENAME_TIMEOUT_MS=45000

# TO TURN THE MODEL PATH ON, two edits in the source, never in the deployed file
# (chezmoi rewrites the deployed copy on the next apply):
#
#   1. Rename this source file to private_provider.env.tmpl.
#   2. Uncomment the matching key line below. Only then does its template
#      expression become live; while this file has no .tmpl suffix chezmoi
#      copies it verbatim and never opens the vault.
#
# The key name is chosen by SMART_RENAME_PROVIDER: OPENAI_API_KEY for openai,
# KIMI_API_KEY for kimi-code, SMART_RENAME_API_KEY for anything else.
#
# OPENAI_API_KEY={{ (keepassxc "OpenAI API").Password }}
#
# ANTHROPIC IS NOT A PROVIDER HERE. The plugin talks OpenAI-compatible HTTP only
# (@ai-sdk/openai-compatible), so an Anthropic key works solely through a
# gateway that speaks that protocol, reached by pointing SMART_RENAME_BASE_URL
# at it and setting SMART_RENAME_API_KEY.
#
# Optional custom naming prompt; a relative path resolves from this directory.
# The default prompt is the plugin's own docs/naming-policy.md.
# SMART_RENAME_PROMPT_PATH=naming-prompt.md
